API-04: return finished statistics in project units from the statistics getters

swmm_getSubcatchStats(), swmm_getNodeStats(), swmm_getStorageStats(),
swmm_getOutfallStats(), swmm_getLinkStats(), swmm_getPumpStats(),
swmm_getSystemRoutingTotals() and swmm_getSystemRunoffTotals() copied the
accumulators of stats.c and massbal.c: averages as sums over routing steps,
times in seconds, depths as volumes, pollutant loads in mg/L x ft3 and every
length, flow and volume in ft, cfs and ft3, also for SI projects. Convert
them as statsrpt.c and massbal.c do for the report: divide sums by the step
or period count, seconds by 3600 (pump utilization by the routed time),
precipitation and runoff-total depths by the area, and apply UCF() and the
pollutant mass factor.

writeFlowClass() also divided LinkStats[].timeInFlowClass in place, so the
getter's value depended on whether the report had been written; it now
divides a copy. The header comments that described values the engine does
not keep (Courant-critical "time", pump off-curve "depth") now describe the
returned values.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-04_swmm530.patch

